  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "Add support for tzinfo parameter to TruncDate(). TruncDate inherits from TruncBase, which includes the TimeZone mixin. This functionality is intended to allow a developer to pass in a tzinfo object for converting date values, but the current implementation unconditionally uses get_current_timezone_name(), discarding any provided tzinfo object. As a result, aggregations by date do not work correctly when a non-default timezone is used. The fix requires that the tzinfo parameter be recognized and properly applied via the get_tzname() method, ensuring that date truncation respects the provided timezone.",
    "hint_texts": "Update the TruncDate class implementation in django/db/models/functions/datetime.py. In the as_sql method (around line 292), replace the existing call that retrieves the timezone name using timezone.get_current_timezone_name() with a call to self.get_tzname(). Ensure that the provided tzinfo parameter is correctly utilized to determine the appropriate timezone for date conversion.",
    "entrypoint": "File: django/db/models/functions/datetime.py; Class: TruncDate; Method: as_sql. Modify the line 'tzname = timezone.get_current_timezone_name() if settings.USE_TZ else None' to 'tzname = self.get_tzname()'.",
